{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403531-dread-powers-of-methuselah-vampires","id":1403531,"title":"Dread Powers of Methuselah Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-19T09:16:03-07:00","id":1403531,"title":"Dread Powers of Methuselah Vampires","content":"\u200bI thought about making Methuselah Vampires more unique. The idea is to give Methuselahs some additional mystery and capability, and to make them more characterful. Criticism and new ideas are welcome!<br /> <br /> Dread Powers<br /> <br /> 4th Generation Vampires can choose two Minor Powers and two Major Powers. 5th Generation Vampires can choose one Minor Power and one Major Power. The Dread Powers manifest within a few years after the Embrace.<br /> <br /> If there is any instance of a person resisting a given power (Storyteller's discretion, mortals should not generally be able to do so), then the Methuselah Vampire gets a dice pool of 9 (4th Generation) or 8 dice (5th Generation) at difficulty three, from which she gathers successes that can then be possibly beaten.<br /> <br /> The time periods given between usage of abilities are rough guidelines.<br /> <br /> Minor Powers<br /> <br /> Ancient Stalker - The Vampire's movements (including the Vampire moving or handling relatively small items) cannot be heard by anyone except the Vampire. She leaves no footprints behind. The Vampire can turn this on and off with a moment of concentration.<br /> <br /> Savor the Feast - the Vampire can discern an amount of information about a person she drinks from. What he has done recently, what are his interests, who he cares about or fears...One area of interest is given per two Blood Points gained from a feeding. This can be used a few times every month.<br /> <br /> Cow the Mortal - with an effort of will and a touch (handshake, hug, a hand on the shoulder etc.) the Vampire drains the lifeforce of a mundane human so that they feel completely exhausted. This is a voluntary action by the Vampire, and can be done through clothes. This Power does work on Ghouls, but not on Mages or Garou. This can be used a few times during each night.<br /> <br /> Dark Insight - the Vampire can read omens. What this means, and how it can be useful, is up to the Storyteller (and the players) . The omens could be: animals (a flock of birds, two stags on a clearing, a single swan seen across a lake etc.), mortal passersby, the weather, discarded or broken items lying around, malfunctions of technology (the streetlight on the corner dimming etc.), overheard conversations.<br /> <br /> Major Powers<br /> <br /> Exalt the Servant - with a small ritual (words exchanged, some item given etc.) the Vampire gifts a Ghoul or a Revenant with the ability to learn out-of-Clan Disciplines, and a single dot of such a Discipline. This can be used once every few years<br /> <br /> Clan Paragon - when used on a Neonate Vampire (specifically - it cannot be a Fledgling or an Ancilla, or an older Vampire) one of the Neonate's Clan Disciplines is increased to five dots This can be used once every twenty years. Note this<i> can</i> be used on Vampires of Clans other than the Methuselah with this Power.<br /> <br /> Dark Enlightenment - the Vampire can bestow the outlook of hers morality to another willing (remember that willing does not exclude being misled) Vampire of a different morality. This results in the Vampire gaining four dots of a Path of Enlightenment, Road, or Humanity, and three in the appropriate Virtues. This can be used once every fifteen years.<br /> <br /> Twilight Walk - if the day is approaching and the Vampire wishes to reach a Haven that she used before, then as long as it is located in the same city, the time passage changes to accommodate the Vampire returning to her Haven. The night is effectively prolonged for the Vampire as long as all that she does is return to her Haven. While returning, the Vampire strangely will encounter no other persons. Time stretches only for the Vampire, anyone else (except possibly persons accompanying the Vampire) is unaffected. This can be used twice every few years.<br /> (How this happens? One explanation could be that the Power is directly influencing the subjective passage of time. Another is that the Vampire walks through the Umbra.)<br /> <br /> Indomitable Intuition - the Vampire can be deductions of frightening sharpness. With minimal information about a person (or an event), the Vampire can predict: which apartment a person will rent (out of a selection), what car will they buy, what items he will take with him on a trip, or to who he will confide to. This can be used a few times every few years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-20-2020, 07:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T11:14:34-07:00","id":1403549,"title":"","content":"Honestly, i don't care overly much for that as they already have Elder powers - and consequently the extra option of Elder Combos - as venues of customization not available for the majority of kindred, PCs or NPCs.<br /> <br /> They already have so many available tools as It stands, i overall care more for enhancing individualization options at the base of the power ladder.<br /> <br /> Seriously, get ONE random canon methuselah NPC, make a list of all possible elder powers it MIGHT have, try to see how many different builds you could make from the combinations. THEN you toy with a list of Discipline Combos/Amalgams/Devotions, to further add to the ball of overpowered crazy.<br /> <br /> Just one discipline set may offer the possibility of dozens of wildly differing custom superpower builds. And how many dozen methuselahs does one need in a chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T20:23:05-07:00","id":1403614,"title":"","content":"Some very similar notions were tossed around on NSH's thread here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1343288-v5-empowering-the-ancient-blood-gods\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ent-blood-gods</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}